    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2050953536498811269",
      "url": "https://x.com/adonispara/status/2050953536498811269",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/adonispara/status/2050953536498811269",
      "text": "> Steve Reeves\n> born in 1926 (Montana, a small town near the Canadian border)\n> father was a rancher, killed in a farming accident when Steve was young\n> mother raised him alone, they moved to Oakland, California when he was 10\n> one day on the route he arm wrestled a boy who lived nearby (a boy smaller than him)\n> the smaller boy won\n> Steve found out the boy trained with weights in his garage\n> Steve started training, then found his way to Ed Yarick's gym in Oakland\n> Yarick became a father figure to Steve\n> steve walked in at 163 lbs\n> four months later he was 193 lbs\n> his genetics were unlike anything Yarick had seen\n> graduated high school 1944, enlisted in the US Army immediately\n> assigned to Company A of the 25th Division, sent to the Philippines\n> his fellow soldiers nicknamed him \"The Shape\"\n> caught malaria in the Pacific, lost 25 lbs\n> during the occupation of Japan he found weights and started building himself back up\n> left the Army September 1946 after 26 months of service\n> walked straight back into Yarick's gym\n> won Mr. Pacific Coast 1946 (his first competition)\n> Won it again 1947 (also took Best Chest, Best Arms and Best Legs the same night)\n> won Mr. America 1947\n> won Mr. World 1948\n> flew to London, won Mr. Universe 1950\n> the night he won Mr. Universe he stood on stage and announced his retirement from bodybuilding\n> moved to New York to study acting under Stella Adler\n> they argued, she refunded his tuition\n> studied elsewhere, started doing vaudeville acts with a comedian named Dick Burney\n> one of Cecil B. DeMille's scouts spotted him\n> DeMille cast him as Samson opposite Hedy Lamarr, told him to lose 15 lbs\n> Steve couldn't do it, they gave the role to Victor Mature\n> the film broke box office records\n> Steve spent years in bit parts going nowhere\n> then an Italian director's daughter pointed to his photo and said \"him\"\n> Steve's fee for Hercules was $10,000\n> by 1960 he was the number one box office draw in 25 countries, ahead of John Wayne\n> Highest paid actor in Europe\n> Turned down James Bond in Dr. No, 1962\n> Turned down the lead in A Fistful of Dollars (the role went to Clint Eastwood)\n> A shoulder injury from a chariot stunt ended his acting career\n> Retired to a ranch, bred horses, invented Powerwalking, campaigned against steroids until he died\n> Died 1 May 2000, aged 74\n\nArnold Schwarzenegger said: \"If I could push a button to look like Steve Reeves in Hercules or Arnold in Conan, I'd push the Steve Reeves button\"",
